Multi-Program Repository
This repository contains several programs written in Assembly and C to demonstrate file handling, statistics computation, multithreading, and socket-based chat systems.

1. # Assembly Program – Count Lines in a File
Description:

Reads a text file in the same directory.

Counts the number of lines in the file (including empty lines).

Prints the total count to the console.

Compile:

nasm -f elf64 question2.asm -o question2.o
ld question2.o -o question2
Run:

./question2
2. # C Extension for Python – Statistics Module
Description:

A Python C extension module to efficiently compute:

Sum of values

Mean

Standard deviation

Mode

Count of values

Move to question3 folder:
cd question3

Build:

python3 setup.py build
Install (locally):

python3 setup.py install --user
Usage in Python:

import stats

data = [1.0, 2.0, 2.0, 3.0]
print(stats.sum_values(data))
print(stats.mean_values(data))
print(stats.std_dev(data))
print(stats.mode_value(data))
print(stats.count_values(data))
3. # Producer-Consumer Simulation (Multithreaded C Program)
Description:

Simulates a manufacturing system using the Producer-Consumer model.

Producer adds items to a shared queue (max size 10).

Consumer removes items from the queue.

Uses pthread and condition variables for synchronization.

Compile:

gcc question4.c -o q4
Run:

./q4
4. # Linux Multithreaded Chat System (Sockets + Threads)
Description:

Server handles up to 4 concurrent clients.

Clients authenticate with a username.

Supports private chat between users.

/list to view online users, /switch to change chat target.

Non-blocking message reception using threads.

First move to question5 folder:
cd question5

Compile Server:

gcc -C chat_server.c -o server 
Compile Client:

gcc -C chat_client.c -o client 
Run Server:

./server
Run Client (in separate terminals):

./client